Now the flow module. Need careful design.

Screens: 'home' | 'setup' | 'sensing' | 'stopped' | 'games' | 'review' | 'sessions' | 'help'.

State:
```ts
export interface ActiveSessionState {
  id: string;
  startedAtEpochMs: number;
  betweenGames: boolean;
  markedGames: number;
}
export interface ReportDraft {
  sessionId: string;
  slots: string[];
}
export interface ReviewState {
  sessionId: string;
  result: ReportResult | null;
  building: boolean;
  error: string | null;
  progress: {scored,total} | null;
  cancelling: boolean;
}
export interface FlowState {
  screen: Screen;
  consent: boolean;
  session: ActiveSessionState | null;
  stoppedSessionId: string | null;
  draft: string[];
  review: ReviewState | null;
  explainerSeen: boolean;
  notice: string;
  error: string | null;
  sdkError: string | null;
}
```
Notice default "The camera stays off until you consent." That's initial. But hydration may have consent; then notice should change. Hydrated event: consent -> if granted "Consent is on. The camera opens when you start sensing." else default.

Events:
```ts
export type FlowEvent =
 | {type:'hydrated'; consent: boolean; session: {id, startedAtEpochMs, betweenGames} | null; explainerSeen: boolean}
 | {type:'explainerDismissed'}
 | {type:'consentChanged'; granted}
 | {type:'sessionStarted'; sessionId; startedAtEpochMs}
 | {type:'sessionStopped'; sessionId; notice}
 | {type:'openHome'}
 | {type:'openSetup'}
 | {type:'openSessions'}
 | {type:'openHelp'}
 | {type:'openStopped'}
 | {type:'openGames'}
 | {type:'openReview'}
 | {type:'pasteChanged'; slots}
 | {type:'reportStarted'; sessionId; slots}
 | {type:'reportProgress'; scored; total}
 | {type:'reportReady'; result}
 | {type:'reportFailed'; message}
 | {type:'reportCancelRequested'}
 | {type:'reportCancelRejected'}
 | {type:'gapChanged'; betweenGames}
 | {type:'openedSession'; sessionId; report: ReportResult | null; games: string[]}
 | {type:'sessionDeleted'; sessionId}
 | {type:'notice'; message}
 | {type:'error'; message}
 | {type:'sdkError'; message}
 | {type:'clearError'}
```
`openGames` requires session: if no `stoppedSessionId` and no `session`, ignore? Games can be opened from stopped only. Determine `currentSessionId(state)`: review?.sessionId ?? stoppedSessionId ?? session?.id. `openGames` allowed from stopped, review, games (no-op). Use guard:
- stopped -> games
- review -> games (keep review? set screen games, keep draft from review slots)
- games -> games.
`openStopped` allowed from games/review and stoppedSessionId present -> stopped.
`openReview` only if review?.result != null; from stopped? Review requires a report. From sessions handled by openedSession.
`reportStarted`: allowed from games; sets screen review, review{building:true,result:null,...}, draft slots.
`reportReady`: only if review.building and sessionId matches; sets result, building false.
`reportFailed`: sets error, building false.
`reportCancelRequested`: cancelling true.
`reportCancelRejected`: cancelling false.
`sessionStopped`: session null, stoppedSessionId=sessionId, screen stopped, review null? If a session stops while reviewing? impossible. Clear draft/review, notice.
`sessionStarted`: screen sensing, session {markedGames:0}, stoppedSessionId null, review null, draft [], error null, notice 'Waiting for a face.'.
`openedSession`: screen review if report != null else games; stoppedSessionId=sessionId; draft=games; review if report {building:false,...} else null; notice maybe.
`sessionDeleted`: if ids match current review or stoppedSessionId -> home with cleared; else no change.
`gapChanged`: only while session exists; set betweenGames; increment markedGames when changing false->true.
`error` sets error; `clearError` null. `notice` sets notice. `sdkError` sets.
`consentChanged`: if false, notice default; if true "Consent is on..."; but don't clear session? Main stops on revoke; sessionStopped will arrive separately. We can just set consent.

Illegal transitions: return same object (identity) when not allowed. Tests assert same state or expected.

`statusFor`:
```ts
export interface StatusInput { error: string|null; sdkError: string|null; screen: Screen; hint: string|null; notice: string|null; }
export function statusFor(input): {text:string; tone:'error'|'warn'|'note'|'default'}
```
Priority: error -> tone error; sdkError -> error; hint (only sensing/setup? plan says sensing) -> note; notice -> default; fallback.
The UI sets role=alert when tone==='error'. Tests.

`sensingHint(samples, validation)` moved from App. It returns string|null and only sensing. Actually current statusLine depends on phase. Make:
```ts
export function sensingHint(samples, validation): string | null {
  if (validation && validation.code !== 0) return validation.hint;
  if (samples.length === 0) return 'Waiting for a face.';
  ...
}
```
Then statusFor with hint.

`initialFlowState(explainerSeen)`.

`stoppedNote`? Keep in App or move? Move `formatNumber` not needed. Keep.

`currentSessionId(state)` export for insight.

Potential circular imports: flow.ts imports contracts types (ReportResult, PulseSample, ValidationMessage) — fine. contracts doesn't import flow.

