content.text:
Now refactor App.tsx. This is the biggest part. We'll rewrite the file substantially. Need to preserve behavior and integrate reducer.

Let's design the new App:

Imports:
- useReducer, useEffect, useRef, useState.
- contracts schemas + types.
- flow functions/types.
- components.

State:
```ts
const [flow, dispatch] = useReducer(flowReducer, false, initialFlowState);
const [samples, setSamples]...
const [selectedIndex]...
const [validation]...
const [coachMessage]...
const [insightState]...
```
Remove `granted`, `timeControl` stays local, `phase`, `sessionId`, `pasteSlots`, `reportResult`, `reportBuilding`, `reportError`, `reportProgress`, `reportCancelling`, `betweenGames`, `gapPending` local? `gapPending` can stay local. `note`, `error`, `sdkError` moved to flow.

Refs: grantedNow, startPending, revokedDuringStart, reportRequestSeq, insightRequestSeq, sessionIdRef, terminalSessionRef, supersededSessions.

Hydration:
```ts
useEffect(() => {
  if (!bridge) return;
  void bridge.getAppState().then(raw => {
    const parsed = appStateSchema.safeParse(raw);
    if (!parsed.success) return;
    dispatch({type:'hydrated', consent: parsed.data.consent.granted, session: parsed.data.session.active && parsed.data.session.sessionId && parsed.data.session.startedAtEpochMs !== null ? {...} : null, explainerSeen: readExplainerSeen()});
  }).catch(() => undefined);
}, [bridge]);
```
Explainer preference: S47 owns it. For S46, pass false (not shown yet). Do not implement explainer. So `explainerSeen: true`? If false, later S47 shows. Keep `localStorage` read as S47? Not now. Use `true` to avoid future accidental? Hmm, S47 will read preference. For now pass `false` but no UI uses it. Fine; hydration overwrites to false. No issue.

Actually if localStorage onboarding dismissed, S47 later needs `readExplainerSeen`. Not this step.

grantedNow ref must sync: in hydration set grantedNow.current = parsed.granted and maybe sessionIdRef. Also set `sessionIdRef` to active id if session. This is important for owner logic. In an effect after hydration:
```ts
grantedNow.current = state.consent;
```
Use another effect watching flow.consent.
And when flow.session changes, sync sessionIdRef? adoptSession does it. Hydration bypasses; set in handler after parsed.

Let's set refs inside the `.then`:
```ts
grantedNow.current = parsed.data.consent.granted;
if (active) { sessionIdRef.current = id; terminalSessionRef.current = null; }
```

Adopt session helper:
```ts
function adoptSession(nextId: string, startedAtEpochMs: number): void {
  resetInsight();
  setCoachMessage(null);
  if (sessionIdRef.current === nextId) return;
  if (sessionIdRef.current) supersededSessions.current.add(sessionIdRef.current);
  sessionIdRef.current = nextId;
  terminalSessionRef.current = null;
  reportRequestSeq.current += 1;
  dispatch({type:'sessionStarted', sessionId: nextId, startedAtEpochMs});
  setSamples([]); setSelectedIndex(null); setValidation(null);
}
```
But for stop we don't want sessionStarted; call:
```ts
function settleSession(meta: SessionMeta, notice: string) {
  resetInsight(); setCoachMessage(null);
  if (sessionIdRef.current && sessionIdRef.current !== meta.id) supersededSessions.current.add(sessionIdRef.current);
  sessionIdRef.current = meta.id;
  reportRequestSeq.current += 1;
  dispatch({type:'sessionStopped', sessionId: meta.id, notice});
  setSamples([]); setSelectedIndex(null); setValidation(null);
}
```
Wait: on stop, samples should maybe stay for the stopped screen strip (currently they stay; adoptSession resets). Current onStop calls adoptSession(meta.id) which resets samples because id differs? sessionIdRef was same id, so adoptSession returns early after resetting insight/betweenGames, and doesn't reset samples. Actually adoptSession if same id returns early, so samples stay. Good. For stop, keep samples. For new session, clear. Let's keep separate `settleSession` that preserves samples and sets stopped state. On auto-end, current adoptSession(parsed.sessionId) if same id returns early (doesn't reset samples), then setPhase stopped; samples stay. So auto-end preserves samples. Good.

So:
```ts
function endSession(meta: SessionMeta, notice: string) {
  resetInsight();
  dispatch({type:'sessionStopped', sessionId: meta.id, notice});
  sessionIdRef.current = meta.id;
}
```
Don't reset samples.

On sessionStarted (new): dispatch; reset state.

`resetInsight` unchanged.

Effects:
- samples: setSamples; dispatch clear? `setSdkError(null)` currently. Dispatch sdkError? There's no clear sdkError event. Add `clearSdkError`? Could dispatch `{type:'sdkError', message:''}`? Bad. Add event `clearSdkError`. Or `clearErrors`. Existing logic clears sdkError on sample and code 0. Add `{type:'clearSdkError'}`.
- validation: local setValidation; if code 0 dispatch clearSdkError.
- sdk error: dispatch sdkError; if !retryable stop...
- sessionEnded: superseded check; dispatch sessionStopped with parsed.message; set sessionIdRef; terminal.
- report progress: check currentSessionId(flow) but effect closure might stale. Use sessionIdRef. Progress only when review building? Dispatch handles guard by `review?.building`, but state in dispatch closure is current. Good. Check `parsed.data.sessionId !== sessionIdRef.current`.
- consent sync effect: `grantedNow.current = flow.consent`.

Status:
```ts
const sessionId = currentSessionId(flow);
const status = statusFor({error: flow.error, sdkError: flow.sdkError, screen: flow.screen, hint: flow.screen === 'sensing' ? sensingHint(samples, validation) : null, notice: flow.notice});
```
Use `status.urgent ? 'alert' : 'status'` and aria-live="polite". Current code had role alert only when error; keep.

Focus effect:
```ts
useEffect(() => {
  const heading = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('main h1');
  if (!heading) return;
  heading.tabIndex = -1;
  heading.focus();
}, [flow.screen]);
```
This runs on mount too; okay, maybe focus on initial load nice. But focusing h1 on every screen change including report building updates? dependency screen only.

Handlers:
- onConsent: uses flow.consent / phase. `revoking = grantedNow.current`. If flow.screen === 'sensing'... Same logic. On success `dispatch consentChanged`, update ref. If revoking and session stops, `settleSession(meta, stoppedNote(meta))`. Note: stop before setConsent; fence logic.
- onStart: `bridge.startSession(timeControl)` returns startedAtEpochMs. adoptSession(id, startedAt). On revocation stop: settleSession. dispatch error via readIpcError.
- onStop: settleSession.
- onGapToggle: uses flow.session?.betweenGames; dispatch gapChanged.
- onInsightRequest: uses sessionId from currentSessionId(flow).
- onPasteContinue: dispatch reportStarted; then bridge.buildReport; dispatch reportProgress/ready/failed. Paste slots from event. Note: `reportRequestSeq` guards.
- onCancelReport: dispatch cancelRequested; call; if !cancelled dispatch cancelRejected.
- openGames: dispatch pasteChanged with slots then openGames. Actually PasteScreen onBack gives current slots; `dispatch({type:'pasteChanged', slots}); dispatch({type:'openGames'})`.
- diagnostics: dispatch notice or error.
- screen render:
  - if screen === 'games': PasteScreen with `sessionId` (still shown; S53 removes), initialSlots flow.draft length>0, onBack: dispatch pasteChanged + openStopped, onContinue.
  - if screen === 'review': review = flow.review. If review.building -> show progress. If review.error -> refusal panel with "Edit games"/"Back to session". If review.result?.ok -> report layout. Otherwise refusal Timeline.
    Current code: `reportResult` null -> "Session timeline" with Timeline null. For build error, reportResult null and error. We'll restructure:
    - building
    - review.error -> "Report unavailable." panel
    - review.result?.ok -> full report
    - review.result (refusal) -> Timeline refusal
    - !review.result && !building && !error -> shouldn't happen; show "No report yet."
    Buttons: Edit pasted PGNs (dispatch openGames), Back to session (dispatch openStopped).
  - else home/sensing/stopped: heading text based on screen; indicator; controls.
    - "Start sensing" when screen !== sensing. Home/stopped/help/etc. But if screen setup later. For now only home/sensing/stopped.
    - Start button disabled={!flow.consent}.
    - Consent button uses flow.consent.
    - Gap control uses flow.session?.betweenGames; show "Game ended (N marked)"? S49 owns the improved control, but now we can display count minimally? S46 shouldn't add feature. Keep current labels, but derive from flow.session.
    - CoachLine shown when sensing && flow.session?.betweenGames.

`statusLine`/`stoppedNote` helpers: remove statusLine; keep `stoppedNote` and formatNumber.

Need `SessionMeta` type import.

Potential issue: `flow.session` null on reload if only preview (S48 later). Fine.

`sessionId` for PasteScreen should be `currentSessionId(flow)`, not live only.

`insight` request: `currentSessionId(flow)` can be review session. Good.

One more: on report build, `reportStarted` sets review; if build result returns but the user navigated away (openGames) then review still exists; reportReady updates review but screen games. That's okay; "openReview" only from stopped though. If user hits Edit games during build, build continues; when done, review has result. But screen games, no path back to review. Current behavior also allowed Edit pasted PGNs while building. We could cancel build on edit? Not required. Keep.

`onPasteContinue` sets slots, but if `!bridge || !sessionId`, dispatch reportStarted with sessionId '' invalid? Better handle before: if no id, dispatch error + openGames. Current code sets phase report with error "No stored session". Implement:
