Now refactor App.tsx. This is the biggest part. We'll rewrite the file substantially. Need to preserve behavior and integrate reducer.

Let's design the new App:

Imports:
- useReducer, useEffect, useRef, useState.
- contracts schemas + types.
- flow functions/types.
- components.

State:
```ts
const [flow, dispatch] = useReducer(flowReducer, false, initialFlowState);
const [samples, setSamples]...
const [selectedIndex]...
const [validation]...
const [coachMessage]...
const [insightState]...
```
Remove `granted`, `timeControl` stays local, `phase`, `sessionId`, `pasteSlots`, `reportResult`, `reportBuilding`, `reportError`, `reportProgress`, `reportCancelling`, `betweenGames`, `gapPending` local? `gapPending` can stay local. `note`, `error`, `sdkError` moved to flow.

Refs: grantedNow, startPending, revokedDuringStart, reportRequestSeq, insightRequestSeq, sessionIdRef, terminalSessionRef, supersededSessions.

Hydration:
```ts
useEffect(() => {
  if (!bridge) return;
  void bridge.getAppState().then(raw => {
    const parsed = appStateSchema.safeParse(raw);
    if (!parsed.success) return;
    dispatch({type:'hydrated', consent: parsed.data.consent.granted, session: parsed.data.session.active && parsed.data.session.sessionId && parsed.data.session.startedAtEpochMs !== null ? {...} : null, explainerSeen: readExplainerSeen()});
  }).catch(() => undefined);
}, [bridge]);
```
Explainer preference: S47 owns it. For S46, pass false (not shown yet). Do not implement explainer. So `explainerSeen: true`? If false, later S47 shows. Keep `localStorage` read as S47? Not now. Use `true` to avoid future accidental? Hmm, S47 will read preference. For now pass `false` but no UI uses it. Fine; hydration overwrites to false. No issue.

Actually if localStorage onboarding dismissed, S47 later needs `readExplainerSeen`. Not this step.

grantedNow ref must sync: in hydration set grantedNow.current = parsed.granted and maybe sessionIdRef. Also set `sessionIdRef` to active id if session. This is important for owner logic. In an effect after hydration:
```ts
grantedNow.current = state.consent;
```
Use another effect watching flow.consent.
And when flow.session changes, sync sessionIdRef? adoptSession does it. Hydration bypasses; set in handler after parsed.

Let's set refs inside the `.then`:
```ts
grantedNow.current = parsed.data.consent.granted;
if (active) { sessionIdRef.current = id; terminalSessionRef.current = null; }
```

Adopt session helper:
```ts
function adoptSession(nextId: string, startedAtEpochMs: number): void {
  resetInsight();
  setCoachMessage(null);
  if (sessionIdRef.current === nextId) return;
  if (sessionIdRef.current) supersededSessions.current.add(sessionIdRef.current);
  sessionIdRef.current = nextId;
  terminalSessionRef.current = null;
  reportRequestSeq.current += 1;
  dispatch({type:'sessionStarted', sessionId: nextId, startedAtEpochMs});
  setSamples([]); setSelectedIndex(null); setValidation(null);
}
```
But for stop we don't want sessionStarted; call:
```ts
function settleSession(meta: SessionMeta, notice: string) {
  resetInsight(); setCoachMessage(null);
  if (sessionIdRef.current && sessionIdRef.current !== meta.id) supersededSessions.current.add(sessionIdRef.current);
  sessionIdRef.current = meta.id;
  reportRequestSeq.current += 1;
  dispatch({type:'sessionStopped', sessionId: meta.id, notice});
  setSamples([]); setSelectedIndex(null); setValidation(null);
}
```
Wait: on stop, samples should maybe stay for the stopped screen strip (currently they stay; adoptSession resets). Current onStop calls adoptSession(meta.id) which resets samples because id differs? sessionIdRef was same id, so adoptSession returns early after resetting insight/betweenGames, and doesn't reset samples. Actually adoptSession if same id returns early, so samples stay. Good. For stop, keep samples. For new session, clear. Let's keep separate `settleSession` that preserves samples and sets stopped state. On auto-end, current adoptSession(parsed.sessionId) if same id returns early (doesn't reset samples), then setPhase stopped; samples stay. So auto-end preserves samples. Good.

So:
```ts
function endSession(meta: SessionMeta, notice: string) {
  resetInsight();
  dispatch({type:'sessionStopped', sessionId: meta.id, notice});
  sessionIdRef.current = meta.id;
}
```
Don't reset samples.

On sessionStarted (new): dispatch; reset state.

