  onBack(): void;
  onHelp(): void;
}
```
- h1 "Set up your session."
- Sections with h2: "1. Camera and consent", "2. Framing", "3. Time control".
- Consent button with aria-pressed. Text: "The camera stays off until you press Allow the camera. Nothing is recorded. No video or image is saved; only pulse numbers are stored on this computer." Matches README.
- Key row: `SmartSpectra key` + status text:
  - present: "Present (value not shown)." or keyDetail (doctor detail "Present (value not shown).").
  - missing: keyDetail (one sentence).
  - loading: "Checking…"
  - error: keyDetail.
  - Use role? Maybe `<p>`.
- Framing:
  - previewSlot (CameraPreview or placeholder)
  - `<ul className="framing-checks">` with 3 `<li>`:
    - "One face in view" + `framingStatusText`
    - "Upper chest visible"
    - "Enough light"
  - `<p className="framing-hint" role="status">` hint:
    - if framing all pass: "Framing looks good."
    - else if framingHint: hint
    - else: "Waiting for the camera to report framing."
  - `framingHint` passed from validation when code != 0; when code 0 -> null.
  - If key missing/consent off, previewSlot maybe placeholder text.
- Time control buttons with aria-pressed.
- Start:
  - `<button className="primary-btn" disabled={!gate.canStart} onClick={onStart}>Start sensing</button>`
  - If canStart: `<p className="setup-ready">All checks pass. Start when you are ready.</p>`
  - Else `<ul className="setup-reasons" aria-live="polite">` reasons as li.
- Back / Help buttons.
- Check rows status text is not color-only.
- Key status "Missing" text; no color needed.

Need server test. CameraPreview not included via previewSlot. Use `previewSlot={<div>Preview</div>}`.
Test with `renderToStaticMarkup`.

Add CSS:
```css
