content.text:
Need to remove setupFocus/refs, add setup state/effects, change dismissExplainer to openSetup.

Imports:
```ts
import { framingFromValidation, framingReady, UNKNOWN_FRAMING, type FramingChecks } from '../shared/framing';
import { keyStatusFromChecks, setupGate, type KeyStatus, type PreviewStatus } from '../shared/setup';
import { setupStatusSchema, previewStartResultSchema, ... } from contracts; 
import { SetupScreen } from './SetupScreen';
```
We need `setupStatusSchema` and `previewStartResultSchema`? Preload validates start result, but App can trust typed bridge. Still parse for boundary? App already parses contracts. Add `setupStatusSchema`.
- `previewStart` returns typed `{started:true}` from preload; no schema needed but could parse. Use bridge types.

State:
```ts
const [setupKey, setSetupKey] = useState<{status:KeyStatus;detail:string}>({status:'loading',detail:'Checking…'});
const [preview, setPreview] = useState<PreviewStatus>('idle');
const [previewError, setPreviewError] = useState<string|null>(null);
const [previewAttempt, setPreviewAttempt] = useState(0);
```
Remove setupFocus/refs.

dismissExplainer:
```ts
function dismissExplainer(startSetup: boolean) {
 remember...
 dispatch(explainerDismissed);
 if (startSetup) dispatch(openSetup);
}
```
- If Start setup from first run, openSetup. Good.

Effects:
1. Setup key status + reset preview when entering setup:
```ts
useEffect(() => {
 if (flow.screen !== 'setup') { setPreview('idle'); setPreviewError(null); return; }
 if (!bridge) { setSetupKey({status:'error',detail:'This page is open outside ChessPulse.'}); return; }
 let alive = true;
 setSetupKey({status:'loading',detail:'Checking…'});
 setValidation(null);
 setPreview('idle');
 setPreviewError(null);
 void bridge.getSetupStatus().then(raw => {
   if (!alive) return;
   const parsed = setupStatusSchema.safeParse(raw);
   if (!parsed.success) { setSetupKey({status:'error',detail:'The key check returned an unexpected result.'}); return; }
   setSetupKey(keyStatusFromChecks(parsed.data.checks));
 }).catch(() => { if(alive) setSetupKey({status:'error',detail:'The key check could not run.'}); });
 return () => { alive = false; };
}, [flow.screen, bridge]);
```
Note: when preview attempt changes, don't recheck key.
2. Preview:
```ts
useEffect(() => {
 if (flow.screen !== 'setup' || !bridge || !flow.consent || setupKey.status !== 'present') {
   return undefined;
 }
 let alive = true;
 setPreview('starting');
 setPreviewError(null);
 setValidation(null);
 void bridge.startPreview().then(() => {
   if (alive) setPreview('running');
 }).catch((caught) => {
   if (!alive) return;
   setPreview('error');
   setPreviewError(readIpcError(caught,'camera_unavailable'));
 });
 return () => {
   alive = false;
   void bridge.stopPreview().catch(() => undefined);
 };
}, [flow.screen, flow.consent, setupKey.status, previewAttempt, bridge]);
```
- On cleanup due to setupKey change from loading->present? The first effect run with status loading returns undefined (no preview); then present starts. Good.
- When consent toggles off, cleanup stops; no new start.
- When `previewAttempt` increments after start failure, cleanup stops then starts.
- `setValidation(null)` on each start; good.
- `startPreview` may have already been called by StrictMode cleanup sequence; controller handles.
3. Key status when leaving setup: key persists; okay.
4. `framing` derive:
```ts
const framing = validation ? framingFromValidation(validation.code) : UNKNOWN_FRAMING;
const gate = setupGate({consent: flow.consent, keyStatus: setupKey.status, keyDetail: setupKey.detail, preview, previewError, framing});
```
- `framingHint`: `validation && validation.code !== 0 ? validation.hint : null`.
- `setupKey` initial loading.
- When key missing, preview effect no-op; gate key reason.
- When key present but consent false, no preview; gate consent reason.
- Start handler:
```ts
async function onStart(): Promise<void> { ... }
```
Currently used by SetupScreen only. It calls `bridge.startSession(timeControl)`. On failure, set preview attempt +1 so effect restarts preview:
```ts
catch (caught) {
 if (...) {
   dispatch(error...);
   setPreview('idle');
   setPreviewAttempt(n=>n+1);
 }
}
```
But if failure is consent revoked, don't restart. Check grantedNow.
- Also when start succeeds and screen changes, preview cleanup stops; fine.
- Should stop preview explicitly before start? Main sessionStart stops it. If main stops it and then fails, attempt restarts. Fine.
- Start button disabled by gate; no need guard, but add if (!gate.canStart) return.
- `onConsent` while on setup: toggles, effect starts/stops preview. Good.
- When consent is revoked, onConsent doesn't stop a session (screen setup), calls setConsent; main onRevoked stops preview; effect cleanup stops. Good.

Focus effect: remove setupFocus effect and refs; `dismissExplainer` no focus. Screen changes to setup after Start setup, focus h1. Good.

Home branch:
- After first-run and help, before games:
```tsx
if (flow.screen === 'home') {
 return <main><label/><h1>Ready when you are.</h1><StatusRegion status={status}/><div actions><button primary onClick={()=>dispatch({type:'openSetup'})}>Start a session</button><button Help/></div></main>
}
```
- What about consent state on Home? Could show a note. Not required. If consent already granted, Setup will skip consent step but still display button pressed. Fine.
- `Start a session` primary.

Setup branch:
```tsx
if (flow.screen === 'setup') {
 const previewSlot = !flow.consent
   ? <p>Allow the camera to see your framing.</p>
   : setupKey.status !== 'present'
     ? null
     : preview === 'running'
       ? <CameraPreview active guide />
       : null;
 return <main><SetupScreen .../></main>
}
```
- Pass `previewSlot` always; if null, no preview.
- `keyDetail`: setupKey.detail.
- `onBack` -> openHome.
- `onHelp` -> openHelp (helpReturn setup, close returns setup; preview effect cleanup on screen change stops preview! Opening Help from Setup stops the camera because effect cleanup. That's okay/privacy, but returning to Setup restarts preview and key check? Key effect deps [flow.screen, bridge] re-runs on return, setting key loading -> preview stops/starts. Fine, though slower. Could keep key. Acceptable.)
- On Help, the camera preview stops (effect cleanup), which is good privacy.
- `SetupScreen` h1.
- Setup status region? SetupScreen shows reasons; global status for errors should appear. Add `<StatusRegion status={status} />` above/after SetupScreen? If status is consent note, it would duplicate. Only show urgent errors: `{status.tone === 'error' ? <StatusRegion status={status}/> : null}` before SetupScreen. On start failure, error appears.
- SetupScreen heading focus: focus effect picks main h1 (inside SetupScreen). Good.

Default sensing/stopped:
- Remove time control group (`!sensing && !stopped` was only home; now home branch handles, so remove).
- Remove Start button (only Sensing/stopped remain; stopped uses Paste). In sensing, show stop/gap; in stopped, Paste. No "Start sensing".
- Consent button keep on sensing/stopped? On stopped, consent can remain; but Home/Setup handle. Keep on sensing for revoke; on stopped maybe show consent state? Simpler: show consent button only while sensing? If stopped, camera off; revoking consent isn't urgent. But user may want to revoke. Keep for both; label.
- Help button keep.
- CameraPreview on sensing: `active={sensing}` (renamed prop).
- On stopped, currently `CameraPreview sensing={false}` if consent; blank preview with caption. Could keep or omit. The stopped screen should show summary, not camera. S48/S50 will polish. Remove CameraPreview when stopped; show only sensing. This avoids a blank preview and privacy confusion. The current stopped screen shows it; changing is okay.
- SensingStrip: show while sensing; stopped could show final trace (useful). Keep strip on both.
- Heading text: sensing "Sensing.", stopped "Sensing stopped.".
- Remove `!sensing && !stopped` time controls.
- Actions:
  - stopped: Paste PGNs primary.
  - sensing: gap + stop.
  - consent button for sensing only? Keep both; if stopped, "Allow the camera" would let consent on; fine.
  - Help.
- "Start sensing" removed from default; Setup has it.

CameraPreview prop rename. Let's do that first.

