Now App sensing integration.

Add imports: `signalQuality, formatElapsedMs, limitWarning` from shared/sensing; `SensingControls`.
State: `const [nowMs, setNowMs] = useState(() => Date.now()); const [confirmingStop, setConfirmingStop] = useState(false);`
Effects:
- Timer when `flow.session?.id`:
```ts
useEffect(() => {
 if (!flow.session) return;
 setNowMs(Date.now());
 const timer = window.setInterval(() => setNowMs(Date.now()), 1000);
 return () => window.clearInterval(timer);
}, [flow.session?.id]);
```
Using `flow.session?.id` in deps is allowed. `flow.session` object in body from render; when gap changes, effect doesn't rerun (dep id). Good.
- Reset confirmingStop when session changes/screen not sensing:
```ts
useEffect(() => {
 setConfirmingStop(false);
}, [flow.session?.id, flow.screen]);
```
This would reset when gap changes? deps id/screen only. On entering sensing set false; good.
- Elapsed:
```ts
const elapsedMs = flow.session ? Math.max(0, nowMs - flow.session.startedAtEpochMs) : 0;
const elapsedLabel = formatElapsedMs(elapsedMs);
const warning = flow.session ? limitWarning(elapsedMs) : null;
const quality = signalQuality(samples);
```
- `onGapToggle` unchanged.
- `onStop` should set confirming false before call? In confirm handler.
- In default sensing render:
  - remove inline indicator `<p className="indicator">Sensing</p>`.
  - after StatusRegion / CameraPreview / SensingStrip / CoachLine, add `{flow.session ? <SensingControls .../> : null}`.
  - The action row currently has gap/stop. Remove those; keep consent/Help.
  - On stopped, actions Paste/consent/Help.
- App-wide indicator component:
  - Create `CameraOpenIndicator.tsx`:
    ```tsx
    export function CameraOpenIndicator({ sensing, preview }: { sensing: boolean; preview: boolean }) {
      if (!sensing && !preview) return null;
      return <p className="camera-status" role="status"><span className="recording-dot" aria-hidden="true"/>{sensing ? 'Sensing' : 'Camera preview'}</p>;
    }
    ```
  - Use in each return as fragment. But adding to 7 branches is tedious. Alternative: render indicator inside a top-level wrapper after computing `screen` but before branches by restructuring? We can define:
    ```tsx
    const cameraIndicator = <CameraOpenIndicator sensing={Boolean(flow.session)} preview={flow.screen === 'setup' && preview === 'running'} />;
    ```
    Then each `return (` needs `<>{cameraIndicator}<main>...`. That's 7 edits.
  - Could instead render the indicator in `main.tsx` outside App? It needs state; no.
  - Could put it inside `StatusRegion`? StatusRegion is rendered in most branches but not all (review? error only; sensing yes; home yes; setup only error; games only error; help yes; first-run yes). Not reliable.
  - Could use a fixed element in the default branch only? "app-wide" means every screen while camera open. Camera is open only on sensing and Setup preview (and Help stops it). Review/Games/Home have no camera. So we only need indicator on:
    - Sensing screen
    - Setup screen while preview running
    - Help screen? Camera is stopped on Help (preview cleanup) and a session Help keeps camera open! Help from sensing keeps the session (indicator needed).
    - Any other screen while session? Games/review only after stop; Home no session. So: sensing, setup, help.
  - Add indicator to those three branches only. But the plan says every screen; those are the possible ones. If a future screen can be reached while sensing, S49 wrapper would help. For now, add a `CameraOpenIndicator` at top of sensing, setup, help. Also first-run/home? No camera.
  - However, if Help from sensing, existing inline indicator in Help currently `<p className="indicator">Sensing</p>`; replace with CameraOpenIndicator.
  - Setup: indicator while preview running.
  - Sensing: indicator.
  - Stopped: no camera; no.
  - This satisfies app-wide for reachable screens. Document.
  - Could define `const cameraIndicator = ...` and include in those returns.
  - Setup `preview` state: if preview starting, no indicator until running. Camera may be opening during starting; a brief gap. Use `preview === 'running' || preview === 'starting'` for indicator to be safe. But "Camera preview" while starting is honest.
  - Help from Setup: preview stops, so no indicator; Help from sensing: session true -> "Sensing".
  - CameraOpenIndicator props `sensing`, `preview` (preview mode active).
- Add CSS already.

Sensing screen text:
- `SensingControls` shows elapsed/quality/warning/gap/stop.
- The StatusRegion above still shows "Sensing." or confidence hint.
- Good.

Stop confirmation handlers:
```tsx
<SensingControls
 elapsedLabel={elapsedLabel}
 limitWarning={warning}
 qualityLabel={quality.label}
 betweenGames={flow.session.betweenGames}
 markedGames={flow.session.markedGames}
 gapPending={gapPending}
 confirmingStop={confirmingStop}
 onGap={() => void onGapToggle()}
 onRequestStop={() => setConfirmingStop(true)}
 onConfirmStop={() => { setConfirmingStop(false); void onStop(); }}
 onKeepSensing={() => setConfirmingStop(false)}
/>
```
- If session null (shouldn't be on sensing), skip.
- `onStop` currently checks screen sensing; yes.
- If confirm and auto-end, screen changes; effect resets.

Elapsed timer wall clock: `flow.session.startedAtEpochMs` from start. On reload hydration, startedAt from main. Good.
- If clock jumps backward, clamp 0; warning not. Fine.
- Timer continues while Help (App stays mounted), but not rendered. Fine.

Add component.

